      "sourceTextSha256": "e25b7da5f3a0ecdff679eca167bffbd70a1b1001561f2b8e16ec85d1e9ab76ba",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw9trov9-0oxzxedywb",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "A full-day group excursion to Machu Picchu, the ‘Lost City of the Incas’, with an English-speaking guide. After the fall of the Inca Empire, the most learned priests retreated to Machu Picchu, which the Spanish never found. The city was built from enormous limestone blocks without mortar on a mountaintop surrounded by dense, impassable jungle. It was discovered by the American archaeologist Hiram Bingham in 1911. Lunch. Return to Cusco by train and transfer to the hotel on arrival."
